Changes the backend CORS configuration from wide-open (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`) to respecting the `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` environment variable.

```diff
- app.use(cors());
+ const allowedOrigins = process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS?.split(",").filter(Boolean) ?? [];
+ app.use(cors({ origin: allowedOrigins.length > 0 ? allowedOrigins : false, credentials: true }));
```

When `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` is unset, CORS is disabled entirely (origin: false) rather than allowing all origins. Set it to a comma-separated list of frontend URLs in production.

AdMob on iOS 14+ requires ATT authorization before serving personalized ads. Without `NSUserTrackingUsageDescription` in the plist and an explicit `requestTrackingAuthorization` call, the system prompt never appears and AdMob defaults to non-personalized ads.

## Changes

### `fire_cap/ios/App/App/Info.plist`
- Added `NSUserTrackingUsageDescription` key with a user-facing tracking rationale string

### `fire_cap/ios/App/App/AppDelegate.swift`
- Imported `AppTrackingTransparency`
- Request ATT authorization in `applicationDidBecomeActive`, gated on iOS 14 availability and `.notDetermined` status to avoid redundant calls on every app foreground

```swift
import AppTrackingTransparency

func applicationDidBecomeActive(_ application: UIApplication) {
    if #available(iOS 14, *) {
        if ATTrackingManager.trackingAuthorizationStatus == .notDetermined {
            ATTrackingManager.requestTrackingAuthorization { _ in }
        }
    }
}
```

> `AppTrackingTransparency` is a system framework — no Podfile changes required. Also ensure `GADApplicationIdentifier` is set in `Info.plist` with your AdMob App ID, as AdMob will crash at launch without it.

## Summary

Adds the first minimal evidence adapter for the agent lab.

This implements issue #3 without changing the upstream SSL contract. The adapter is input-driven: lookup starts from `CandidateEvidenceRequest`, not from a weightless seed object.

Closes #3 when merged.

## Upstream relation

This PR does not dynamically fetch or duplicate upstream SSL logic.

Instead, it treats `E-AI-MODEL/shadowseed` as the canonical SSL source for:

- seed lifecycle;
- trace/weight separation;
- Validation Gate behavior;
- contradiction handling;
- promotion semantics;
- evidence discipline.

This adapter sits before the upstream-compatible Validation Gate. It prepares candidate `EvidenceRef` objects from input/context. A later gate step decides whether those refs support promotion.

## What changed

- Add `shadowseed_agent_lab/evidence_adapter.py`
- Add package exports in `shadowseed_agent_lab/__init__.py`
- Add fixture corpus at `examples/agent_lab/fixtures/evidence_corpus.json`
- Add tests in `tests/test_evidence_adapter.py`

## Boundary

The adapter may:

- accept input/context through `CandidateEvidenceRequest`;
- return `EvidenceRef` objects;
- distinguish verified fixture evidence from generated output;
- filter refs eligible for the later Validation Gate.

The adapter may not:

- accept a seed object as lookup driver;
- assign seed weight;
- assign seed status;
- promote a seed;
- replace the Validation Gate.

## Alignment with golden path

This PR follows the merged golden path:

```text
input/context
  -> candidate-evidence lookup
  -> verified evidence refs

seed candidate
  -> weightless seed

weightless seed + verified evidence refs
  -> Validation Gate
```

## Tests

```bash
python -m unittest discover -s tests
```

Covered tests:

- lookup is input-driven;
- weightless seed dict is rejected as lookup driver;
- generated output is not verified gate evidence;
- verified fixture evidence is returned;
- unverified evidence does not support the gate;
- adapter does not assign weight, status, or promotion.

Esta PR adiciona a etapa de baseline CNN 2D, análise visual de erros e interpretabilidade com Grad-CAM.

Principais entregas:
- treinamento e avaliação da CNN 2D;
- notebook 05 com resultados do baseline CNN;
